# The root R0 without an entry. Both properties of the physical word in one context (the coordinates of Sol and Astra
# for the row construction_index_word): the physical `A[0]` keeps the word B, and the named path to B gives a
# Structure. `Use` has the reference input `@: target`; its body writes through it. `Use\go(D\B)` -- the named path is
# a Structure: admitted, `D\B\v` 8. `Use\go(D\A[0])` -- the physical `A[0]` is the word B, not a Structure: the
# reached admission refuses, 4; `Log\before` 1, `Log\after` 0.
@: Log (int: before 0; int: after 0)
@: D (B(int: v 7); A(B); @: p A[0])
@: Use (
    @: target
    go:
        target\v := target\v + 1
    end: go
)
Log\before := 1
Use\go(D\B)
Use\go(D\A[0])
Log\after := 1
